2880
03:04:56,640 --> 03:05:02,240
In India, I remember wanting to wear hijab at my cousin's wedding and everyone kept saying,

2881
03:05:02,320 --> 03:05:04,840
Are you going to wear a dupatta at the wedding?

2882
03:05:04,920 --> 03:05:10,680
The bride, my cousin's sister, even kept begging me not to wear it because it was her day.

2883
03:05:10,760 --> 03:05:15,040
My parents weren't there and the pressure was just too much, so I gave in and I didn't wear it.

2884
03:05:15,120 --> 03:05:20,160
I still regret that and it's one more reason I'm so grateful for the space I get in Saudi Arabia.

2885
03:05:20,300 --> 03:05:26,880
As for the gifts, the couple was going to live with the groom's parents for a few years so they didn't need household items.

2886
03:05:26,960 --> 03:05:32,760
Most people just gave a fixed amount of money and if someone couldn't, it was totally fine.

2887
03:05:32,840 --> 03:05:42,460
Some gave coins or gold biscuits to the bride instead of loads of necklaces because our generation doesn't wear that much gold and coins are a better investment anyway.

2888
03:05:42,540 --> 03:05:44,340
My mic is working.

2889
03:05:44,420 --> 03:05:46,700
I really want my my own wedding to be like this.

2890
03:05:46,850 --> 03:05:50,767
Even more, I'd love a small Nikkah in Medina, just with my parents, my family,

2891
03:05:50,847 --> 03:05:54,770
